# Rebased response_ttl patch for the dae package of kenzok8/openwrt-daede.
#
# The mirror ships upstream's own 010-dns-response-ttl.patch, which was written
# against the 2026.09.12 source snapshot. The dae-src rolling release keeps only
# the newest three tarballs, so pin-daede-source.py must adopt a newer asset as
# soon as upstream rotates one out -- and upstream's patch then no longer
# applies. On 2026.09.19 every hunk touching control/dns_control.go,
# config/config.go and cmd/run_shutdown_test.go was rejected, because upstream
# split NormalizeAndCacheDnsResp_ out into control/dns_controller_cache.go,
# moved the runtime tunables into control/dns_controller_runtime.go, and stopped
# rewriting A/AAAA answers to TTL 0 altogether.
#
# This rebase keeps the option's documented contract: response_ttl > 0 pins the
# TTL dae advertises to downstream clients for address answers, while 0 keeps
# dae's default, i.e. forwards the upstream TTL. The override runs after the
# cache entry lifetime has been derived from the real record TTLs, so the packed
# entry replays with the remaining part of the override and the TTL a client
# sees no longer depends on whether the entry happened to be cached.
#
# The option has to live in the binary: config/parser.go rejects unknown keys
# ("unexpected key: %v"), so a config carrying response_ttl would leave dae
# unable to start if the patch were dropped instead.
#
# Regenerate against a new rotation with:
#   tar --strip-components=1 -C src -xzf dl/dae-src-<version>-<id>.tar.gz
#   cp -a src a && cp -a src b      # apply the edits to b/, then:
#   diff -ruN a b > 010-dns-response-ttl.patch
#
# Verify a rebase before pushing. The tree ships a dae_stub_ebpf build tag
# precisely so the control package can be type-checked and tested without
# bpf2go, which needs clang and the generated eBPF objects:
#   patch -p1 --dry-run --forward -d src/core < 010-dns-response-ttl.patch
#   cd src/core
#   go build -tags dae_stub_ebpf ./config/... ./control/...
#   go test  -tags dae_stub_ebpf -count=1 ./control/ ./cmd/
# This rebase was checked that way: build clean, control suite green with zero
# failures (identical to the unpatched tree) and TestDnsController_
# ResponseTtlOverride proving that 0 keeps the upstream TTL while a positive
# value pins it.
#
# Verified against dae-src-2026.09.19-183975cdc1d2, -336134cbfade and
# -c34592141905.
